This version calls `GetField(126)` directly and returns `FIT_FLOAT32_INVALID` if the field is missing. That skips the generic dispatch on the sub-field index inside `GetFieldFLOAT32Value`.

It should return the same values only if the SDK's `GetFieldFLOAT32Value` is a null check followed by a direct call to the field when given `FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD`. I wrote this from memory of the SDK and have not checked it against the actual source, and I have not measured the speedup.

```cpp
    FIT_FLOAT32 GetEnhancedAvgAltitude(void) const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(126);
        if (field == FIT_NULL)
            return FIT_FLOAT32_INVALID;
        return field->GetFLOAT32Value(0, FIT_SUBFIELD_INDEX_MAIN_FIELD);
    }
```